' ============================================================================
' 31 Recorded embeddings: rho:vectordb:embed in play and in replay.
'
' Source of Figure N16.3 in ../design.md (section N16). The figure restates
' embed, embed_reply, embed_texts and produce_recorded of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/system_processes.rs, the quota and
' the reply codes of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/vectordb_services.rs,
' and the recorded processes of non_deterministic_ops() in
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/system_processes.rs (decisions 52, 57, 58 and
' 68). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. Play on the proposer: the process checks the shape and the quota of
'      the texts, asks the embedder of the node, and replies.
'   2. The dispatcher records the whole reply on the produce event of the
'      reply, a failure reply included.
'   3. The program sends a record with embedding=, so the vector is
'      consensus state from then on.
'   4. Replay on another node produces the recorded reply and asks no
'      embedder, so the two nodes compute the same state.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 31-recorded-embeddings.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 31-recorded-embeddings
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ActorBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
}
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Recorded embeddings: rho:vectordb:embed (decisions 57 and 68)
autonumber

participant "Program\n(a deploy)" as PROG $rrs_host
participant "rho:vectordb:embed\n[0xE0, 0x24]" as EMBED $rrs_system
participant "Embedder of the node\n(all-MiniLM-L6-v2, 384)" as MODEL $rrs_service
participant "Event log\n(the produce event of the reply)" as LOG $rrs_substrate
participant "VectorDB space\n(consensus state)" as SPACE $rrs_storage

== Play on the proposer ==
PROG -> EMBED : embed!(ret, "a text")  or  embed!(ret, [text...])
EMBED -> EMBED : check the shape: one text, or a list of texts\n(else the reply [false, "BadArgument", ...])
EMBED -> EMBED : check the quota: at most 64 texts and 64 KiB\n(else the reply [false, "EmbeddingRateLimited", ...])
EMBED -> MODEL : embed(texts)
MODEL --> EMBED : one vector of f32 values for each text
EMBED -> LOG : produce the reply on ret\n[true, vector, model], or [true, [vector...], model]
note right of LOG
  The dispatcher records the whole reply,
  a reply [false, code, detail] included,
  because the process is a recorded process
  (non_deterministic_ops()).
end note
LOG --> PROG : the reply
PROG -> SPACE : docs!(text; embedding=vector)
SPACE -> SPACE : OFFER-VDB the record with its embedding:\nit fires a waiter, or the space stores it\n(consensus state from now on)

== Replay on another node ==
PROG -> EMBED : the same call, in replay
EMBED -> LOG : produce the recorded reply on ret
note over MODEL
  Replay asks no embedder. Two nodes with
  other models compute the same state.
end note
LOG --> PROG : the recorded reply
PROG -> SPACE : the same send, with the same embedding

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_host>       | the program of the deploy |
|<$rrs_system>     | the system process |
|<$rrs_service>    | the node service outside consensus |
|<$rrs_substrate>  | the event log of the deploy |
|<$rrs_storage>    | the records of the space |
endlegend
@enduml
